  "_form": "The claim about DA-6's compact dressing. Same discipline as contract/PIN: the four files are DATA, this is the CLAIM about them, and the check needs no JSON parser to run. The shape, though, is assets/terrain/tiles/PIN's and not contract/PIN's -- `files` plus a `fetched` block -- because that is the shape tools/fetch_artefacts.py reads. contract/PIN describes ONE COMMITTED file and carries `file_sha256`, singular, with no `fetched` block at all; a pin in its literal shape would be fetched by nothing and would report no error saying so.",
